WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.060 --> 00:00:05.880
Love affairs, violent outbursts, and the&nbsp;
spit seen 'round the world… Some movies&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:05.880 --> 00:00:09.660
are best known for the crazy things that&nbsp;
happened while the cameras weren't rolling.

00:00:09.887 --> 00:00:14.100
"Don't Worry Darling" had been garnering&nbsp;
hype since Olivia Wilde first signed on&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:14.100 --> 00:00:19.260
to direct and Florence Pugh and Harry Styles&nbsp;
were cast as the leads. It seemed likely to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:19.260 --> 00:00:24.240
be one of the most anticipated movies of&nbsp;
2022 since its announcement, but gossip&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:24.240 --> 00:00:28.320
has been following the film's production&nbsp;
since the start of principal photography.

00:00:28.320 --> 00:00:32.760
Wilde split with her longtime&nbsp;
fiancé Jason Sudeikis — with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:32.760 --> 00:00:37.020
whom she shares two kids — while she&nbsp;
was working on the film. Rumors of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:37.020 --> 00:00:40.440
her new relationship with Styles&nbsp;
were confirmed not long after.

00:00:40.440 --> 00:00:45.360
There was also an awkward conflict&nbsp;
between Olivia Wilde and Shia LeBeouf,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:45.360 --> 00:00:49.800
who was originally slated to star.&nbsp;
Wilde told Variety that the former&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:49.800 --> 00:00:54.060
"Transformers" star was fired because of the&nbsp;
"combative energy" of his acting process,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:54.060 --> 00:00:58.740
while LeBeouf denied this claim and said that&nbsp;
he quit because Wilde didn't give the actors&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:58.740 --> 00:01:04.380
enough time to rehearse. Then there was Pugh,&nbsp;
who uncharacteristically refused to promote the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:04.380 --> 00:01:08.340
film on her Instagram while Wilde was&nbsp;
enthusiastically singing her praises.

00:01:08.340 --> 00:01:12.840
Everything came to a head at the film's&nbsp;
Venice Film Festival premiere in September&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:12.840 --> 00:01:18.780
2022. Pugh didn't show up for the Q&amp;A, Wilde&nbsp;
and Pugh avoided each other on the red carpet,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:18.780 --> 00:01:23.580
and there was a whole conspiracy theory&nbsp;
that Styles may have spit on Chris Pine&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:23.580 --> 00:01:27.902
at the premiere — which Wilde denied on&nbsp;
"The Late Show with Stephen Colbert."

00:01:27.902 --> 00:01:31.770
"Harry did not spit on Chris,&nbsp;
in fact, but that did—"

00:01:31.770 --> 00:01:32.386
"Only time will tell."

00:01:32.386 --> 00:01:34.500
"No, I pro— he really didn't!"

00:01:34.500 --> 00:01:35.248
"Well…"

00:01:35.248 --> 00:01:36.660
"He d— hahaha!"

00:01:36.660 --> 00:01:40.500
Pugh has declined to comment directly&nbsp;
on the rumors of her feud with Wilde,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:40.500 --> 00:01:44.986
but she did finally post about the film on&nbsp;
her Instagram, praising the film's crew.

00:01:45.000 --> 00:01:50.700
When "Blade" came out in 1998, it put Marvel&nbsp;
on the map in a new way thanks to Wesley&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:50.700 --> 00:01:56.160
Snipes' turn as an extremely cool vampire.&nbsp;
By the time of the release of 2004's "Blade:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:56.160 --> 00:02:00.720
Trinity," Snipes' star had faded —&nbsp;
and according to actor Patton Oswalt,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:00.720 --> 00:02:05.100
this was partially because of his antics&nbsp;
on set. In an interview with The A.V. Club,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:05.100 --> 00:02:10.560
Oswalt revealed that filming "Blade: Trinity" was&nbsp;
one of the worst work experiences he's ever had.

00:02:10.560 --> 00:02:16.440
According to Oswalt, Snipes refused to film most&nbsp;
of the movie, meaning that a body double had to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:16.440 --> 00:02:21.960
be used for a number of scenes. Snipes also&nbsp;
allegedly got into verbal and physical fights&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:21.960 --> 00:02:27.180
with writer-director David Goyer and insisted on&nbsp;
staying in character throughout the production.

00:02:27.180 --> 00:02:30.900
"He would only answer to the name&nbsp;
Blade, you couldn't call him…"

00:02:30.900 --> 00:02:32.580
"He would only answer to Blade?!"

00:02:32.580 --> 00:02:33.240
"To Blade, yeah."

00:02:33.240 --> 00:02:35.100
In an interview with The Hollywood Reporter,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:35.100 --> 00:02:39.780
Goyer neither confirmed nor denied&nbsp;
Oswalt's claims, but said that "Blade:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:39.780 --> 00:02:46.080
Trinity" had a troubled production. Wesley Snipes&nbsp;
spoke to The Guardian in 2020 and denied Oswalt's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:46.080 --> 00:02:50.880
allegations while wondering why people were so&nbsp;
inclined to believe Oswalt in the first place.

00:02:50.880 --> 00:02:57.000
Ryan Reynolds — who also starred in the&nbsp;
film — told IGN in 2012 that the rumors&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:57.000 --> 00:03:02.640
about tension on set were "overblown" and that&nbsp;
he respects Snipes' method process. Regardless,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:02.640 --> 00:03:05.040
"Blade: Trinity" was panned by critics,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:05.040 --> 00:03:10.159
and is mostly remembered for solidifying&nbsp;
Snipes' reputation as a difficult actor.

00:03:10.440 --> 00:03:14.760
Brad Pitt and Jennifer Aniston&nbsp;
announced their separation in 2005,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:14.760 --> 00:03:19.380
but both parties insisted that the split&nbsp;
had nothing to do with the tabloid reports&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:19.380 --> 00:03:24.420
of his relationship with Angelina Jolie. When&nbsp;
Pitt and Jolie were photographed on vacation&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:24.420 --> 00:03:28.800
together just a month after the divorce&nbsp;
was finalized, the Hollywood heartthrob&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:28.800 --> 00:03:33.360
found himself at the center of one of the&nbsp;
biggest Hollywood scandals of the 2000s.

00:03:33.360 --> 00:03:40.140
It all started with 2005's "Mr. and Mrs. Smith,"&nbsp;
a decent enough action flick that stars Pitt and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:40.140 --> 00:03:46.020
Jolie as married undercover spies tasked with&nbsp;
killing each other. Pitt and Jolie met on set,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:46.020 --> 00:03:50.820
and rumors that they were having an affair&nbsp;
immediately began to swirl. Jolie spoke to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:50.820 --> 00:03:55.620
Vogue in 2006, claiming that she and&nbsp;
Pitt didn't consider a relationship&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:55.620 --> 00:04:01.080
until the end of the shoot in 2004, but&nbsp;
the damage of the rumors was already done.

00:04:01.080 --> 00:04:06.360
Every celebrity tabloid on the newsstands&nbsp;
was covered in paparazzi photos of Jolie and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:06.360 --> 00:04:11.340
Pitt. According to Entertainment Weekly, the&nbsp;
public obsession with the high-profile love&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:11.340 --> 00:04:16.440
triangle was so huge that Doug Liman, the&nbsp;
director of "Mr. and Mrs. Smith," needed to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:16.440 --> 00:04:20.460
hire extra security units to block the&nbsp;
paparazzi from interrupting the shoot.

00:04:20.460 --> 00:04:25.020
Despite Pitt's efforts to deny that his&nbsp;
relationship with Jolie had led to his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:25.020 --> 00:04:29.820
divorce from Aniston, tabloids spent the&nbsp;
better part of the next ten years looking&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:29.820 --> 00:04:34.500
for ways to resurrect the drama. The film&nbsp;
itself, despite bringing in nearly half&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:34.500 --> 00:04:39.887
a billion dollars at the box office, hasn't&nbsp;
had the same lasting impact as the scandal.

00:04:39.900 --> 00:04:47.160
While 2016's "Suicide Squad" was a commercial hit,&nbsp;
it didn't fare so well with the critics. For many,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:47.160 --> 00:04:51.360
the drama surrounding the film's cast has&nbsp;
easily become the most memorable thing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:51.360 --> 00:04:55.920
about the movie. Jared Leto is famous&nbsp;
for his intense style of method acting,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:55.920 --> 00:05:00.480
and boy did he go for it while in&nbsp;
character as The Joker for "Suicide Squad."

00:05:00.480 --> 00:05:05.100
Some of the film's stars revealed that&nbsp;
Leto — or "The Joker," rather — had given&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:05.100 --> 00:05:09.120
them some rather upsetting gifts. Adam&nbsp;
Beach, who played Slipknot in the film,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:09.120 --> 00:05:14.940
told E! News that Leto sent a live rat to&nbsp;
Margot Robbie and bullets to Will Smith,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:14.940 --> 00:05:19.800
while Viola Davis confirmed to Vanity Fair&nbsp;
that he also sent the cast a dead pig.

00:05:19.800 --> 00:05:25.440
In 2017, Leto told Entertainment Weekly&nbsp;
that he didn't actually give these gifts,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:25.440 --> 00:05:30.060
and lamented how the rumors got out of&nbsp;
hand. However, he had already bragged&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:30.060 --> 00:05:34.800
about his inappropriate presents in an&nbsp;
interview with E! Entertainment in 2016.

00:05:35.000 --> 00:05:41.540
"The Joker is somebody who doesn't really respect&nbsp;
things like personal space or boundaries."

00:05:41.540 --> 00:05:46.380
David Ayers' final cut of the film never&nbsp;
ended up being shown in theaters, and the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:46.380 --> 00:05:51.300
vast majority of Leto's performance as The Joker&nbsp;
was cut from the film. At the end of the day,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:51.300 --> 00:05:56.701
Leto traumatized his co-stars for the sake&nbsp;
of about seven minutes of total screen time.

00:05:56.701 --> 00:05:59.220
"Jared has gone full Joker. Jared,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:59.220 --> 00:06:03.463
he went— he went full Joker, you know. And&nbsp;
the rule generally is never go full Joker."

00:06:03.480 --> 00:06:08.340
Award-winning director David O. Russell&nbsp;
has a reputation for being difficult on&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:08.340 --> 00:06:12.060
set — especially with his actors.&nbsp;
During his time in the industry,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:12.060 --> 00:06:17.580
he's become notorious for his alleged physical&nbsp;
and verbal abuse of cast and crew members.

00:06:17.580 --> 00:06:22.440
One of the most infamous instances of this&nbsp;
behavior occurred on the set of Russell's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:22.440 --> 00:06:28.620
2004 film "I Heart Huckabees," a dark comedy&nbsp;
centering on existential detectives played by&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:28.620 --> 00:06:34.380
Dustin Hoffman and Lily Tomlin. Russell got at&nbsp;
least two massive screaming matches with Tomlin,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:34.380 --> 00:06:37.620
one of which was captured&nbsp;
on a profanity-laden video.

00:06:37.620 --> 00:06:42.840
Tomlin expressed her frustration that Russell&nbsp;
kept contradicting himself with his actor notes,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:42.840 --> 00:06:48.480
which made it hard to know what to do in the&nbsp;
scene. Russell responded by exploding with anger,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:48.480 --> 00:06:53.400
throwing around props, and screaming&nbsp;
misogynistic insults at Tomlin. The video&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:53.400 --> 00:06:57.600
went viral and became the first thing that&nbsp;
many people came to associate with the film.

00:06:57.600 --> 00:07:02.580
Tomlin, like many other actors who have worked&nbsp;
with Russell, has since claimed that there's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:02.580 --> 00:07:08.134
no bad blood between them — but she also hasn't&nbsp;
worked with him again since "I Heart Huckabees."

00:07:08.134 --> 00:07:14.340
Ah, "Fifty Shades of Grey." Originally written&nbsp;
as "Twilight" fan-fiction, the steamy book was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:14.340 --> 00:07:20.580
a sweeping sensation that turned author E.L.&nbsp;
James into the highest-paid writer of 2013.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:20.580 --> 00:07:24.840
That's why it was hardly a surprise when the&nbsp;
rights were optioned for a screen adaptation.

00:07:24.840 --> 00:07:30.180
Rumors swirled about who would play the leads&nbsp;
of Anastasia Steele and Christian Grey until&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:30.180 --> 00:07:35.400
it was finally announced that Dakota Johnson&nbsp;
and Charlie Hunnam had been cast. However,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:35.400 --> 00:07:40.380
Hunnam soon backed out due to scheduling&nbsp;
conflicts and was replaced by Jamie Dornan.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:40.380 --> 00:07:44.760
Once the movie's press tour began, it&nbsp;
became clear that Johnson and Dornan&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:44.760 --> 00:07:49.920
had no sexual chemistry — or even much&nbsp;
affection for each other at all. Any film&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:49.920 --> 00:07:54.360
would suffer if its two leads didn't have&nbsp;
on-screen chemistry, but it was a special&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:54.360 --> 00:07:59.201
kind of disaster for a movie completely&nbsp;
centered on such an intimate relationship.

00:07:59.330 --> 00:08:01.269
"You're up for it if there are two more films?"

00:08:01.701 --> 00:08:03.838
"I… yeah."
"Yeah, are you up for it?"

00:08:03.838 --> 00:08:07.092
"No… bye…"
"Gotta go!"

00:08:07.394 --> 00:08:10.980
The film was critically panned,&nbsp;
but Johnson and Dornan stuck it&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:10.980 --> 00:08:15.120
out to make two more sequels based on the&nbsp;
books. Johnson told Vanity Fair in 2022 —

00:08:30.275 --> 00:08:35.280
"Death on the Nile '' is the second film in&nbsp;
Kenneth Branagh's on-screen revival of Agatha&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:35.280 --> 00:08:41.400
Christie's famous detective Hercule Poirot.&nbsp;
Like his first Poirot film — 2017's "Murder&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:41.400 --> 00:08:45.960
on the Orient Express" — Branagh's "Death&nbsp;
on the Nile" also relied on an all-star&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:45.960 --> 00:08:51.420
ensemble cast featuring Gal Gadot, Armie&nbsp;
Hammer, and Letitia Wright, among others.

00:08:51.420 --> 00:08:56.700
Unfortunately, the film was in post-production&nbsp;
when Hammer — who plays a prominent character&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:56.700 --> 00:09:01.200
in the film — was accused by several&nbsp;
women of sexual violence, adultery,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:01.200 --> 00:09:06.600
and having a cannibalism fetish. Other stars&nbsp;
of "Death on the Nile" also found themselves&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:06.600 --> 00:09:11.820
in hot water: Wright faced scrutiny after&nbsp;
re-tweeting an anti-COVID vaccine video,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:11.820 --> 00:09:16.320
while Gadot received backlash for leading&nbsp;
the tone-deaf effort of celebrities singing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:16.320 --> 00:09:20.640
John Lennon's "Imagine" at the start of&nbsp;
COVID. Gadot also came under fire for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:20.640 --> 00:09:25.200
her controversial statements about the&nbsp;
Israeli-Palestinian conflict in 2021.

00:09:25.200 --> 00:09:30.180
It's tough to sell a movie that depends&nbsp;
on the appeal of its ensemble cast when&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:30.180 --> 00:09:35.400
many of the members of that cast are not looking&nbsp;
so great in the public eye. Maybe the studio&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:35.400 --> 00:09:39.600
will get lucky with a less controversial&nbsp;
ensemble the next time Kenneth Branagh&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:39.600 --> 00:09:45.000
adapts a Poirot story for the screen. That is&nbsp;
if the series isn't already dead in the water.

00:09:45.540 --> 00:09:49.140
Kristen Stewart was at the height of&nbsp;
her "Twilight" popularity when she&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:49.140 --> 00:09:54.960
filmed 2012's "Snow White and the Huntsman," a&nbsp;
gritty live-action interpretation of the Snow&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:54.960 --> 00:09:59.760
White fairy tale. While the film made it through&nbsp;
production and premiered without any major issues,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:59.760 --> 00:10:05.040
things took a turn during the press tour&nbsp;
in the summer of 2012. That was when US&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:05.040 --> 00:10:10.740
Weekly published photos of Stewart and the film's&nbsp;
director Rupert Sanders passionately embracing.

00:10:10.740 --> 00:10:16.800
A director and his leading lady stepping out for&nbsp;
a smooch isn't too terribly shocking — even if&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:16.800 --> 00:10:21.660
he is 19 years her senior — but at the&nbsp;
time, Sanders was married with kids,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:21.660 --> 00:10:25.800
and Stewart was still involved with her&nbsp;
"Twilight" co-star Robert Pattinson.

00:10:25.800 --> 00:10:30.060
"Snow White and the Huntsman" was released&nbsp;
in between the last two installments of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:30.060 --> 00:10:34.140
"Twilight" film saga, and thousands&nbsp;
of fans who had been so excited to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:34.140 --> 00:10:38.700
see Bella and Edward fall in love in real&nbsp;
life were devastated by the revelation.

00:10:38.700 --> 00:10:43.740
Both Sanders and Stewart apologized and&nbsp;
referred to it as a momentary lapse in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:43.740 --> 00:10:48.840
judgment, but the damage was already done.&nbsp;
Sanders and his wife divorced, Stewart and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:48.840 --> 00:10:53.520
Pattinson called it quits for good just a few&nbsp;
months after the photos went public, and one&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:53.520 --> 00:10:58.740
of the biggest Hollywood scandals of the year&nbsp;
overshadowed yet another mediocre action flick.

00:10:58.740 --> 00:11:02.940
Neither Sanders nor Stewart was&nbsp;
invited back to work on the sequel.

00:11:02.940 --> 00:11:06.900
"They didn't put me in that movie because I&nbsp;
went through, you know, such a highly publicized&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:06.900 --> 00:11:10.723
scandal, so they were, like, scared of touching—&nbsp;
yeah, they were scared of touching that."

00:11:10.740 --> 00:11:15.480
It's difficult to understand exactly&nbsp;
what Fox executives were thinking when&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:15.480 --> 00:11:19.920
they signed off on Bryan Singer as the&nbsp;
director for their Freddy Mercury biopic,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:19.920 --> 00:11:24.480
"Bohemian Rhapsody," back in 2016.&nbsp;
By the time the movie began shooting,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:24.480 --> 00:11:29.280
Singer had not only found himself accused&nbsp;
of knowing about and facilitating Kevin&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:29.280 --> 00:11:34.500
Spacey's sex crimes but was also accused of&nbsp;
committing sexual assault against several minors.

00:11:34.500 --> 00:11:39.300
Despite Spacey's public accusations and&nbsp;
subsequent exile from Hollywood's elite,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:39.300 --> 00:11:43.200
Bryan Singer managed to avoid the&nbsp;
same level of scrutiny for some time,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:43.200 --> 00:11:47.520
despite being implicated in and&nbsp;
accused of many similar crimes.

00:11:47.520 --> 00:11:52.440
According to The Hollywood Reporter, Singer's&nbsp;
attendance on the "Bohemian Rhapsody" set was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:52.440 --> 00:11:58.260
erratic at best, and he allegedly was in frequent&nbsp;
conflict with the star of the film, Rami Malek.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:58.260 --> 00:12:03.600
Fox decided to fire Singer with just two weeks&nbsp;
left of filming, but even though he wasn't there&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:03.600 --> 00:12:07.680
to wrap up the film, "Bohemian Rhapsody"&nbsp;
will forever be tainted by his involvement.

00:12:07.680 --> 00:12:11.340
Malek won an Academy Award for&nbsp;
his role as Freddy Mercury,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:11.340 --> 00:12:17.280
and the film enjoyed massive financial success.&nbsp;
For many, however, "Bohemian Rhapsody" will be&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:17.280 --> 00:12:21.720
remembered as having been mostly directed&nbsp;
by an unreliable, unprofessional director,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:21.720 --> 00:12:26.940
who had been accused of sexual assault&nbsp;
by several men long before he was hired.

